.* TCPADM: the task menu for TCP/IP administration.
:PNLGRP.
:COPYR.(C) COPYRIGHT QUARTZ SYSTEMS 2026.
:CLASS NAME=OPTCL BASETYPE='CHAR 2'.
:ECLASS.
:CLASS NAME=NAMECL BASETYPE='CHAR 10'.
:ECLASS.
:VAR NAME=OPTION CLASS=OPTCL.
:VAR NAME=PANELID CLASS=NAMECL VALUE='TCPADM'.
:IMPORT NAME=CFGTCP PNLGRP=QHTOCCMD.
:IMPORT NAME=CFGTCPAPP PNLGRP=QHTOCCMD.
:IMPORT NAME=NETSTAT PNLGRP=QHTONCMD.
:IMPORT NAME=PING PNLGRP=QHTONCMD.
:IMPORT NAME=SNDTCPSPLF PNLGRP=QHTMCMD.
:IMPORT NAME=STRTCPFTP PNLGRP=QHTMCMD.
:IMPORT NAME=WRKACTJOB PNLGRP=QHWMCMD.
:KEYL HELP='KEYS/MENUKEYS' NAME=MENUKEYS.
:KEYI KEY=ENTER ACTION=ENTER.
:KEYI KEY=HELP ACTION=HELP.
:KEYI KEY=F1 ACTION=HELP.
:KEYI KEY=F3 ACTION=EXIT.F3=Exit
:KEYI KEY=F4 ACTION='RETURN 4'.F4=Prompt
:KEYI KEY=F9 ACTION=RETRIEVE.F9=Retrieve
:KEYI KEY=F12 ACTION=CANCEL.F12=Cancel
:EKEYL.
:PANEL NAME=TCPADM HELP=HLPTCPADM KEYL=MENUKEYS ENTER='RETURN 1' TOPSEP=SYSNAM PANELID=PANELID.TCP/IP Administration
:MENU DEPTH='*' SCROLL=YES OPTIONS=OPTION.Select one of the following:
:MENUI HELP=CFGTCP OPTION=1 ACTION='CMD CFGTCP'.Configure TCP/IP
:MENUI HELP=CFGTCPAPP OPTION=2 ACTION='CMD CFGTCPAPP'.Configure TCP/IP applications
:MENUI HELP=NETSTAT OPTION=7 ACTION='CMD NETSTAT'.Work with TCP/IP network status
:MENUI HELP=PING OPTION=8 ACTION='CMD ?PING'.Verify TCP/IP connection
:MENUI HELP=STRTCPFTP OPTION=9 ACTION='CMD ?STRTCPFTP'.Start TCP/IP FTP session
:MENUI HELP='TCPADM/OPT10' OPTION=10 ACTION='CMD ?STRTCPTELN'.Start TCP/IP TELNET session
:MENUI HELP=SNDTCPSPLF OPTION=11 ACTION='CMD ?SNDTCPSPLF'.Send TCP/IP spooled file
:MENUI HELP=WRKACTJOB OPTION=20 ACTION='CMD WRKACTJOB SBS(QSYSWRK)'.Work with TCP/IP jobs in QSYSWRK subsystem
:EMENU.
:CMDLINE SIZE=LONG.Selection or command
:EPANEL.
:HELP NAME=HLPTCPADM.TCP/IP Administration - Help
:P.The TCP/IP stack and its servers: their configuration, their status and
the clients that use them.
:P.Type an option number or a command and press Enter. F4 prompts the
command, F9 brings the previous one back, F12 returns to the menu shown
before this one.
:EHELP.
.* Item, key and option help.
:HELP NAME='KEYS/MENUKEYS'.Function keys
:PARML.
:PT.F3=Exit
:PD.Ends the display and returns to where it was started from.
:PT.F4=Prompt
:PD.Prompts the command on the command line, or the command of the
option typed.
:PT.F9=Retrieve
:PD.Puts the last command run back on the command line; press it again
for the one before.
:PT.F12=Cancel
:PD.Returns to the previous display without acting on what was typed.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='TCPADM/OPT10'.Start TCP/IP TELNET session
:P.Option 10. Runs the STRTCPTELN command&colon. Start TCP/IP TELNET
session.
:EHELP.
:EPNLGRP.
